# Reproduction for bd inc-6sm3, part (b): a polymorphed PC that picks a spit
# attack from the use menu (U). Before the fix, Player::UseMenu's ATTK_VAL
# switch (src/Skills.cpp) had no A_SPIT case and logged "Unimplemented PC
# polymorph attack!"; after it, the spit fires like a breath: a direction
# prompt, then EV_SATTACK.
#
# Read by tools/check_use_menu_skills.sh with the kobold rogue fixture loaded
# (INCURSION_LOAD), so the first key is a game command.
#
#   w y, Polymorph the PC -> Spiders -> Spitting spider
#       the acquisition list shows the highlighted entry on its middle line and
#       the next one below it, so @until stops one DOWN short of the entry.
#   Monster Summoning -> Kobolds -> kobold, one square west
#       a target. The spit is a ray in a direction; with the target adjacent
#       the engine prints "Your poison cloud strikes a kobold."
#   u -> Spit Weapon -> LEFT
#       @expect fails the run (exit 6) if the polymorph did not happen or the
#       entry is absent from the menu.
w
y
@choose "Polymorph the PC"
@until "]: Spiders" RIGHT
@until "Spitting spider" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@while "-- more --" ENTER
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Kobolds"
@choose "kobold"
LEFT ENTER
@while "-- more --" ENTER
u
@expect "Use which skill, feat or ability?"
@expect "Spit Weapon"
@dump:spit-menu
@choose "Spit Weapon"
LEFT
@dump:spit-fired
@while "-- more --" ENTER
@quit
